# The part of the site that is identical in every TLS posture (ADR-0090).
#
# Imported from *inside* the site block of each deploy/Caddyfile.d/<TLS_MODE>.caddy, so this file
# holds site directives only: no site address, no global options, and nothing about TLS. Those are
# exactly the three things a posture changes, and keeping them out of here is what lets the proxy
# configuration exist once instead of in four copies that drift.

encode zstd gzip

# `/internal/*` is the cloud's own trusted-network surface and is NOT part of the public one.
# Those handlers require the X-Pos-Internal-Key shared secret (ADR-0097), which is a second control
# and not a replacement for this deny — they are
# documented as private-network-only (`/internal/ingest` is the reconciliation re-push,
# `/internal/reconcile` the id-diff endpoint, `/internal/ota/report` the fleet report). Nothing
# enforced that assumption: this file used to proxy every path, so all three were reachable,
# unauthenticated, from the internet — event injection, an id-holding oracle, and falsifiable fleet
# state for any tenant. This is the enforcement.
#
# `handle` blocks are mutually exclusive and matched most-specific-first, so the deny cannot be
# reordered behind the proxy by a later edit. It answers **404**, not 403: a 403 confirms the route
# exists, and an internal surface should tell an unauthenticated caller nothing at all.
#
# A deployment that genuinely needs to reach these (a fork running its own cloud-side tooling from
# another host) opens them on the private network, never here. The store's own reporting rides the
# authenticated store surface (`/sync/stores/{id}/…`), where the cloud resolves the tenant from the
# scoped key rather than trusting a body field.
handle /internal/* {
	respond 404
}

# Everything else is the public surface. pos_cloud speaks plain HTTP on :8080 inside the network.
# Active health checks against /health take the upstream out of rotation if the app stops answering,
# so Caddy returns 502 rather than proxying into a dead process.
handle {
	reverse_proxy pos_cloud:8080 {
		health_uri /health
		health_interval 10s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
